{%- comment -%}
  AI Visibility - visible content (PRD-AI-READABILITY P0.1, P0.2, P1.1).

  What the app wrote for a product - summary, facts, who it suits, buyer
  questions - printed as text on the page itself. Every AI system that reads
  a store reads rendered text: the crawlers that build training data, the
  ones that build search indexes, and the agents that fetch a page when a
  user asks. JSON-LD in the head and the plain-text mirror under the app
  proxy reach none of them reliably; this does.

  One snippet so the markup exists once. Rendered by the automatic embed
  (blocks/ai-visibility-content.liquid) and by the block a merchant places
  by hand (blocks/product-content.liquid). A rendered snippet sees only what
  it is given, so both pass the page object and their own settings:

    kind            'product' or 'collection'. Passed, not inferred: a
                    product reached through /collections/x/products/y has a
                    collection in context as well as a product.
    product         the product, when kind is 'product'
    collection      the collection, when kind is 'collection'
    shop_url        shop.url
    heading         the merchant's text; when blank, the default heading in
                    the storefront's language is printed instead
    heading_level   'h2' or 'h3'; questions sit one level below it
    show_summary, show_facts, show_fit, show_questions, show_links
    hidden_groups   the dictionary group labels the facts list leaves out,
                    from shop.metafields['$app'].facts_display (the shop object
                    is not visible inside a rendered snippet, so it is passed)
    our_product_node  theme_scan.ourProductNode: true when the last theme scan
                    found our complete Product node on the product page, which
                    is what the facts fragment below adds to

  Rules, all from the PRD and CLAUDE.md:
  - Renders nothing at all - no wrapper, no heading, no whitespace - unless
    at least one part has content and is switched on. A heading over an
    empty box, or a box holding only two links, is the "0 facts" line the
    merchant was promised never to see.
  - Every value through `escape`: a fact reading "<30 cm & light" prints as
    text, never as markup.
  - Inline styles are spacing, a max-width and the two-column layout of the
    facts list, which P0.1 names. No font, no colour: the block takes the
    theme's own, so it reads as part of the page, not as an advert.
  - No JavaScript, no request, nothing that executes.
  - Every fixed string comes from the extension's locale files through the t
    filter (locales/en.default.json, locales/ro.json), so a Romanian
    storefront prints Romanian around the Romanian text the app wrote.
    Theme app extensions carry storefront locale files for "the text that
    appears in the storefront when your app block or app embed block is
    rendered": https://shopify.dev/docs/apps/build/online-store/theme-app-extensions/configuration
    (Locale files). The t filter itself:
    https://shopify.dev/docs/storefronts/themes/architecture/locales/storefront-locale-files
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign av_h = 'h2' -%}
{%- assign av_hq = 'h3' -%}
{%- if heading_level == 'h3' -%}
  {%- assign av_h = 'h3' -%}
  {%- assign av_hq = 'h4' -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if kind == 'product' and product -%}
  {%- assign av_summary = product.metafields['$app'].summary.value -%}
  {%- assign av_facts = product.metafields['$app'].facts.value -%}
  {%- assign av_fit = product.metafields['$app'].fit_for.value -%}
  {%- assign av_questions = product.metafields['$app'].questions.value -%}

  {%- assign av_show_summary = false -%}
  {%- if show_summary and av_summary != blank -%}{%- assign av_show_summary = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Groups the merchant switched off on the Dictionary screen ("Show on the
    product page") are left out of this list only; they stay in the facts
    metafield, the plain-text page and llms.txt. Counted first, so a product
    whose every fact is hidden prints no empty list.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign av_hidden = hidden_groups -%}
  {%- assign av_visible_facts = 0 -%}
  {%- if show_facts and av_facts -%}
    {%- for fact in av_facts -%}
      {%- unless av_hidden contains fact.k -%}{%- assign av_visible_facts = av_visible_facts | plus: 1 -%}{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign av_show_facts = false -%}
  {%- if av_visible_facts > 0 -%}{%- assign av_show_facts = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign av_show_fit = false -%}
  {%- if show_fit and av_fit != blank -%}{%- assign av_show_fit = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign av_show_questions = false -%}
  {%- if show_questions and av_questions and av_questions.size > 0 -%}{%- assign av_show_questions = true -%}{%- endif -%}

  {%- if av_show_summary or av_show_facts or av_show_fit or av_show_questions -%}
    {%- assign av_heading = heading -%}
    {%- if av_heading == blank -%}{%- assign av_heading = 'content.heading_product' | t -%}{%- endif -%}
    <section class="ai-visibility-content" style="margin:2rem 0;max-width:72rem;">
      <{{ av_h }} style="margin:0 0 0.75rem;">{{ av_heading | escape }}</{{ av_h }}>
      {%- if av_show_summary -%}
        <p style="margin:0 0 1rem;">{{ av_summary | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if av_show_facts -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Label and value exactly as stored in $app.facts, in the stored order,
          which is the order the plain-text mirror prints them in.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <dl class="ai-visibility-content__facts" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(8rem,max-content) 1fr;gap:0.25rem 1.5rem;margin:0 0 1rem;">
          {%- for fact in av_facts -%}
            {%- unless av_hidden contains fact.k -%}
            <dt style="margin:0;">{{ fact.k | escape }}</dt>
            <dd style="margin:0;">{{ fact.v | escape }}</dd>
            {%- endunless -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </dl>
        {%- comment -%}
          The facts in structured data, published by the block that prints them
          (CC-PROMPT-AI-READABILITY-4 item 1), like FAQPage below. The head block
          stopped publishing them on 11 September 2026 (bdef342) because it
          cannot see whether this list is on the page; Google: "Don't mark up
          content that is not visible to readers of the page",
          https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/sd-policies.
          Here, and only here, the list is known to be shown, and exactly
          which facts are in it: a group switched off on the Dictionary screen
          is left out of both.

          A Product fragment: @context, @type, the @id our complete node in the
          head carries, our marker and additionalProperty. Nothing else, so it
          describes no second product - it adds to the one node sharing its
          @id. Emitted only when that node exists: `our_product_node` is the
          theme scan's reading of the product page it last fetched, true when
          our complete Product node was on it (full mode, or extend mode on a
          theme with no Product node). A rendered block cannot see the head
          embed's mode or whether that embed is on, so this is behaviour
          observed on the storefront rather than a setting read. Unknown -
          no scan yet, the password page, a scan from before this flag - is
          not true, and emits nothing: a lone fragment would be a second,
          incomplete Product.

          Never under the theme's @id. The theme scan stores the @id of the one
          product page it read, so that value names a different product on
          every other page, and extend mode on a theme with an @id adds
          nothing to the theme's node. Nothing a theme publishes is therefore
          ever written into: our fragment merges only with our own node, which
          carries no additionalProperty of its own, so an existing
          additionalProperty is never overwritten (the WordPress rule,
          _shopify/IDEAS-FROM-WORDPRESS.md section 7).

          The separator is assigned inside the loop, not `forloop.last`: the
          last fact can be a hidden one, and a comma before the closing
          bracket is invalid JSON that every parser drops silently.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if our_product_node == true -%}
          <script type="application/ld+json">
            {
              "@context": "https://schema.org",
              "@type": "Product",
              "@id": {{ shop_url | append: product.url | append: '#product' | json }},
              "https://mrdigital.ro/ns/ai-visibility": "1",
              "additionalProperty": [
                {%- assign av_ap_sep = "" -%}
                {%- for fact in av_facts -%}
                  {%- unless av_hidden contains fact.k -%}
                  {{ av_ap_sep }}{ "@type": "PropertyValue", "name": {{ fact.k | json }}, "value": {{ fact.v | json }} }
                  {%- assign av_ap_sep = "," -%}
                  {%- endunless -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              ]
            }
          </script>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if av_show_fit -%}
        <p style="margin:0 0 1rem;">{{ 'content.suits' | t }}: {{ av_fit | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if av_show_questions -%}
        {%- for qa in av_questions -%}
          <{{ av_hq }} style="margin:1rem 0 0.25rem;">{{ qa.q | escape }}</{{ av_hq }}>
          <p style="margin:0 0 0.5rem;">{{ qa.a | escape }}</p>
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          FAQPage, here and only here: right after the questions it describes,
          and only when they are shown, so the markup never describes text the
          page does not carry (P0.3). The head block used to emit it whatever
          this block showed. No rich result follows from it - Google ended FAQ
          rich results on 7 May 2026 - and nothing in this app may imply one;
          it is for the reader parsing the page.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <script type="application/ld+json">
          {
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "FAQPage",
            "https://mrdigital.ro/ns/ai-visibility": "1",
            "mainEntity": [
              {%- for qa in av_questions -%}
                {
                  "@type": "Question",
                  "name": {{ qa.q | json }},
                  "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ qa.a | json }} }
                }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
              {%- endfor -%}
            ]
          }
        </script>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if show_links -%}
        <p style="margin:1rem 0 0;"><a href="{{ shop_url }}/apps/ai-visibility/{{ product.handle }}">{{ 'content.plain_text_page' | t }}</a></p>
        <p style="margin:0.25rem 0 0;"><a href="{{ shop_url }}/apps/ai-visibility/llms.txt">{{ 'content.all_products' | t }}</a></p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Collection pages (P0.2): summary, what to choose between, buyer questions,
  then the comparison table, in that order. A collection has no plain-text
  page of its own, so only the index link is offered. Same empty rule: one
  switched-on part with content, or nothing at all.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if kind == 'collection' and collection -%}
  {%- assign av_c_summary = collection.metafields['$app'].summary.value -%}
  {%- assign av_c_criteria = collection.metafields['$app'].criteria.value -%}
  {%- assign av_c_questions = collection.metafields['$app'].questions.value -%}
  {%- assign av_c_table = collection.metafields['$app'].table.value -%}

  {%- assign av_show_summary = false -%}
  {%- if show_summary and av_c_summary != blank -%}{%- assign av_show_summary = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign av_show_criteria = false -%}
  {%- if show_criteria and av_c_criteria and av_c_criteria.size > 0 -%}{%- assign av_show_criteria = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign av_show_questions = false -%}
  {%- if show_questions and av_c_questions and av_c_questions.size > 0 -%}{%- assign av_show_questions = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign av_show_table = false -%}
  {%- if show_table and av_c_table and av_c_table.columns.size > 0 and av_c_table.rows.size > 0 -%}{%- assign av_show_table = true -%}{%- endif -%}

  {%- if av_show_summary or av_show_criteria or av_show_questions or av_show_table -%}
    {%- assign av_heading = heading -%}
    {%- if av_heading == blank -%}{%- assign av_heading = 'content.heading_collection' | t -%}{%- endif -%}
    <section class="ai-visibility-content" style="margin:2rem 0;max-width:72rem;">
      <{{ av_h }} style="margin:0 0 0.75rem;">{{ av_heading | escape }}</{{ av_h }}>
      {%- if av_show_summary -%}
        <p style="margin:0 0 1rem;">{{ av_c_summary | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if av_show_criteria -%}
        <ul style="margin:0 0 1rem;padding-left:1.25rem;">
          {%- for item in av_c_criteria -%}
            <li>{{ item | escape }}</li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if av_show_questions -%}
        {%- for qa in av_c_questions -%}
          <{{ av_hq }} style="margin:1rem 0 0.25rem;">{{ qa.q | escape }}</{{ av_hq }}>
          <p style="margin:0 0 0.5rem;">{{ qa.a | escape }}</p>
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- comment -%} FAQPage after the questions it describes, as on product pages. {%- endcomment -%}
        <script type="application/ld+json">
          {
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "FAQPage",
            "https://mrdigital.ro/ns/ai-visibility": "1",
            "mainEntity": [
              {%- for qa in av_c_questions -%}
                {
                  "@type": "Question",
                  "name": {{ qa.q | json }},
                  "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ qa.a | json }} }
                }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
              {%- endfor -%}
            ]
          }
        </script>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if av_show_table -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The caption is the title with a translated suffix appended, not an
          interpolated translation: the table snippet escapes the caption, and
          a title already escaped by t would come out as "&amp;amp;".
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign av_caption_suffix = 'content.comparison_caption_suffix' | t -%}
        {%- assign av_caption = collection.title | append: av_caption_suffix -%}
        <div style="margin:1rem 0 0;">
          {%- render 'ai-visibility-table', table: av_c_table, caption: av_caption, shop_url: shop_url -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if show_links -%}
        <p style="margin:1rem 0 0;"><a href="{{ shop_url }}/apps/ai-visibility/llms.txt">{{ 'content.all_products' | t }}</a></p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
